  - run-record: 2026-08-31T0411Z-intel: duration_seconds=13655 (~3.8 h) exceeded the runaway threshold — see the per-run watchdog note  [acknowledged 2026-09-06: Reviewed by the 2026-09-06 quality audit, which measured the cause rather than accepting the number: across all seven fires in the 2026-08-30 to 2026-09-06 window, research, composition and the mechanical gate completed in 0.6 to 1.3 h, and the Phase 5.7 verification loop accounted for 60 to 79 % of each fire's wall clock. Not one fire in the window reached a confirmed CLEAN, so every loop ran to or near the 8-iteration cap at a mean of about 11 minutes per iteration. The overrun is therefore the verification gate doing its job at length, not a stalled container and not a runaway workload, and the findings it produced were overwhelmingly genuine: this audit's own retrospective truth passes found only 2 factual errors across 51 published entries. Run records are immutable and the duration is a historical fact. Deliberately NOT fixed by raising the runaway threshold: the check exists to catch the container-stall class (76.8 h, 53.2 h, 11.3 h on record), and moving the line to accommodate a legitimately long verifier loop would blind it to that. Whether the threshold should be recalibrated now that a converged fire is structurally a 3 h fire is raised as operator recommendation 5 instead, because it is a judgement the audit should not make alone. This fire is the window's longest at 3.8 h: all eight iterations returned NEEDS_FIXES and it published on the cap fail-open with eight residuals.]
