  - run-record: 2026-09-09T1726Z-intel: run 2026-09-09T1726Z-intel: verification.iterations missing or empty  [acknowledged 2026-09-13: Reviewed by the 2026-09-13 quality audit. The fire published two entries with an empty verifier block because the pinned Sonnet cti-verification definition was terminated by the content-safety classifier ([cyber]) on all four attempts of the retry ladder — the initial spawn, a defensive-role reframe, a minimal pointer-only message, and a fourth carrying no offensive vocabulary at all, with scope handed via a work/-dir manifest. All four request ids are on the record. That is the documented Phase 5.7 fail-open working as written ('a spawn still blocked after the retry ladder -> publish anyway and note it; never block the run record; a failed spawn never counts as CLEAN'), and the record fabricated no verdict: verification_iterations is the true count, 0. Run records are immutable, so no fix can reach it. This audit independently reproduced the trip THREE more times on the same two entries across three further framings (full batch, reframed, narrowest two-file scope) — seven blocked spawns across two fires — which establishes the trip as a reproducible property of that content against the Sonnet safeguards rather than a message-framing problem, and is reported as the window's headline systemic finding. The verification the waiver deferred was carried out: this audit's main agent re-verified both entries against MSRC, CISA KEV and the cited primaries (batch D). Deliberately NOT fixed by auto-passing a run whose confirmation_waived is non-null: that would let any fire mute the verifier gate with its own prose. The check now carries store severity for this one error under --all only (immutable history -> WARN, the same shape as check_verification_confirmation's store_mode); in run scope it remains a FAIL, so no future fire can publish an empty verifier block without the gate stopping it.]
